&lt;li&gt;Work with labs to automate their experiments end-to-end with Claude - from advising, to prototyping, to writing production code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive product, engineering and research direction based on field experience - e.g. building evals to measure limitations of our models in the physical world (capabilities and safety), developing new features on MHS, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale your impact to the long tail of labs through reusable cookbooks, documentation, and other assets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be an EMEA ambassador for Claude in the lab - you’ll both inspire and build trust with scientific audiences, from small settings to large conferences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role will require significant travel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Might Be a Good Fit If You Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience connecting software to lab robots and instruments (liquid handlers, plate readers, scheduling software, LIMS), ideally in an automated lab.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong engineering skills: you can take an LLM-powered tool from prototype to production code, and write evals to measure its performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A scientist&#39;s instinct for how experiments work: you can spot what&#39;s worth automating, and where AI might fail or be unsafe in the physical world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with external customers or partners in a technical role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication: you’ll write docs other labs can use without you and give talks that inspire and earn researchers&#39; trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A scrappy mentality–comfortable wearing multiple hats, building from scratch, driving clarity in ambiguous situations, and doing whatever it takes to further the mission.&lt;/li&gt;
