&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;About The Team:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Planning team is the most data-driven team at HelloFresh: we plan, schedule and analyse the production of every box, and start the process of feeding the UK. With hundreds of thousands of customers relying on us to get the plan right, this is a role with real ownership and real impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Be Doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting into the site leadership, you&#39;ll own the production plan for the UK in its entirety, and lead the planning team. This is a role for someone who wants to build and elevate: to take a team through a step change in maturity, drive it to operate at its full potential, and make the plan as efficient and optimised as it can be. In your first year you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the UK production plan end to end, working daily with the site director to balance efficiency, plan attainment, minimised downtime and flexibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the planning structure for the site, and take full responsibility for scale hiring of our operational workforce, assessing labour requirements continuously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the ramp and the seasonal calendar, planning ahead rather than reacting to it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach and elevate the planning team, the CS4 Planning Manager and the planning executives, holding them to the level their roles are set at and developing them towards it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously improve the planning strategy, using data and feedback to adapt to changing business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with BI, Operations and wider stakeholders to automate processes, refine planning tools, and move work that shouldn&#39;t sit with the team away from it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate and analyse weekly and monthly KPIs across operational planning, identify trends and issues, and drive cost-saving initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own compliance for the team across Food Safety, Health &amp;amp; Safety and applicable standards (e.g. BRCGS, ISO).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong background in production or labour planning, with proven experience forecasting labour and production needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real people-leadership experience: you&#39;ve managed a team and coached individuals through their development, and you know how to raise a team&#39;s performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong technical skillset, advanced in Excel and Google Sheets, with an understanding of AI and how to apply it to planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Long-term orientation above all: you plan and build for the future rather than firefight, and hold a clear view of where the team and the plan need to be.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven, with the analytical depth to base decisions on fact rather than instinct.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong advocate for your team, able to protect and develop them while raising the bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A degree in supply chain management or a related field is preferable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will get in return:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;● 70% off HelloFresh or Green Chef boxes&lt;br&gt;● Company pension scheme&lt;br&gt;● Gym membership&lt;br&gt;● Bupa private medical insurance (including dental &amp;amp; family cover options)&lt;br&gt;● Mental health first aiders and an employee assistance programme&lt;br&gt;● Nursery support scheme&lt;br&gt;● Cycle to work scheme&lt;br&gt;● Group Life Assurance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;: The Windmill, Unit 2 SmartParc, Derby, DE21 7HW&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be considered for this role, you’ll need to have the independent right to work in the UK, as we&#39;re unfortunately unable to provide sponsorship at this time.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Hybrid Working Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We offer a hybrid working policy for eligible roles, allowing flexibility to work from home and in the office. For more details on eligibility and how this applies to the role you&#39;re applying for, please consult with your recruiter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Next steps&lt;/strong&gt;: Your application will be reviewed and if successful, a member of the Talent Acquisition Team will be in touch within 2 weeks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are required to cooperate with HelloFresh in all health and safety matters. You are responsible for ensuring you take reasonable care of your own health, and safety as well as others who may be affected by the work activities you undertake. You must report incidents immediately and actively raise health and safety-related concerns to your Line Manager.&amp;nbsp;As part of our commitment to maintaining a safe and secure environment, we will process Disclosure and Barring Service (&lt;span class=&quot;il&quot;&gt;DBS&lt;/span&gt;) checks to the successful individual. Failure to disclose relevant information at application or throughout the process could affect your employment with the company.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are currently a HelloFresh employee, please make sure you have discussed your application with your Line Manager.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For over 20 years, Smartsheet has empowered teams to manage work seamlessly and scale solutions smarter. Now, in our most ambitious chapter yet, we are uniting human teams with AI agents. By orchestrating the work agents do best, automating manual tasks and uncovering insights at scale, we create the space for people to focus on what truly matters: judgment, creativity, and big thinking. That is magic at work, and it’s what we show up for every day.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Smartsheet is looking for a regional &lt;strong&gt;Principal Channel Account Manager&lt;/strong&gt; for EMEA based in London. The primary focus will be to optimize, activate and recruit our &lt;strong&gt;French, Middle Eastern &amp;amp; Southern European channels&lt;/strong&gt; by managing and recruiting new solution partners. The channel account manager is a quota-carrying, revenue-producing role that is responsible for recruiting, onboarding and managing relationships with a defined portfolio of partners. The role is responsible for selective new partner recruitment against our ideal partner profile, engaging partners with the Smartsheet Aligned partner program, and driving joint partner business planning. Channel Account Managers will also significantly collaborate with Smartsheet direct sales teams locally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based at Smartsheet in &lt;strong&gt;London, UK (hybrid working cadence)&lt;/strong&gt; and reports to our &lt;strong&gt;Sr, Director - Partner Sales.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the multi-quarter and annual planning process with key partners, spanning enablement, co-marketing, sales pipeline, channel pipeline and forecast reporting; host QBRs and direct the actions that follow from them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive monthly partner alignment sessions, review pipelines, conduct win/loss analysis and direct account penetration strategy to build new sales opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the development of Smartsheet&#39;s EMEA partner strategy, defining which partner types, markets and segments the region pursues next, rather than recruiting against an existing profile&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the acknowledged authority on partner types across the region, including Service Partners, VARs, Referral Partners, Distributors, System Integrators and ISVs, and shape how that mix evolves as the region matures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the build out of a new partner segment or route to market for EMEA, taking it from concept through to a repeatable, revenue-generating motion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and grow partnerships in France, MEA and Southern Europe with accountability for how the model scales into new markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceed revenue targets by developing and maintaining relationships with potential and existing channel partners, and evangelise Collaborative Work Management as an emerging category to new partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the enablement and co-marketing agenda that direct sales, sales engineers and channel marketing follow, rather than coordinating with them as equal stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide input into partner strategy that other CAMs and regions adopt, establishing formal cross-functional networks that coordinate partner activity across the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide sales coaching and enablement, and hold partner organisations accountable for completing required training and certifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct the partner marketing plan with partners and the partner marketing manager, setting the strategy that drives demand against revenue targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the procurement relationship with our distributor, QBS in all relevant territories, including sign off on partner pricing, terms and deal structure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform other duties as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8 to 10 years of sales experience in Enterprise Application software. SaaS experience preferred. Understanding of a services led partner model, where the core value proposition for partners is delivering their own professional services. Not license transactions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability with partner recruitment and joint business planning.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to drive cross-functional teaming&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently resides in the greater London area. Willingness to commute into central London with some regularity, but not daily.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in French is desirable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Legally eligible to work in the UK on an ongoing basis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Perks &amp;amp; Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer-paid Private Medical and Dental, additional cost for family members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly contributions toward your pension&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly stipend to support your work and productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days paid for Holiday + Bank Holidays + Flexible Time Away Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;20 weeks fully paid Maternity Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12 weeks fully paid Paternity/Adoption Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personal paid Volunteer Day to support our community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities for professional growth and development including access to Udemy online courses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company Funded Perks including a counseling membership, salary sacrifice options, and your own personal Smartsheet account.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Teleworking options from any registered location in the UK (role specific)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Get to Know Us:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Smartsheet, your ideas are heard, your potential is supported, and your contributions have real impact. You’ll have the freedom to explore, push boundaries, and grow beyond your role. We welcome diverse perspectives and nontraditional paths—because we know that impact comes from individuals who care deeply and challenge thoughtfully. When you’re doing work that stretches you, excites you, and connects you to something bigger, that’s magic at work. Let’s build what’s next, together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Smartsheet is an Equal Opportunity (EEO) employer committed to fostering an inclusive environment with the best employees. It is our policy to provide equal employment opportunities to all qualified applicants in accordance with applicable laws in the US, UK, Australia, Germany, Costa Rica, Japan, Bulgaria, India, and Singapore. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, protected veteran or disabled status, or genetic information.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If there are preparations we can make to help ensure you have a comfortable and positive interview experience, please let us know.&lt;/p&gt;
